  "about": "The eligible-role strings of the Stats dictionary (26 Aug 2026), as QML's parser reads them, each mapped to the roles of QML's Role vocabulary (Part A AD-104, AD-114, LC-A1-15). An empty list means the string names an input or a note that no slot binds, never a job. A string this table does not hold is listed in the port's unmapped-role report for review and is never guessed. 'management' maps to exit: managing an open trade decides when and where it closes. 'sizing input' beside a stop, target or invalidation maps to no role: the sizer reads that stop or target, so the entry fills an exit slot, never the sizer slot. An entry is a sizer only when its own string claims sizing or risk ('source-native risk claim').",
